Package: sempredict
Type: Package
Title: Out-of-Sample Prediction Assessment for Structural Equation Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nicholas P.", "Danks", email = "nicholasdanks@iss.nthu.edu.tw", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6902-2708")),
    person("Pratyush N.", "Sharma", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3913-0390")))
Description: One assessment layer for out-of-sample prediction across
    covariance-based SEM fitted with 'lavaan' and PLS or consistent PLS (PLSc)
    fitted with 'seminr'. Turns any fitted model into case-level predictions by
    either of two constructions, the construct-score chain used by PLSpredict or
    the model-implied regression of de Rooij et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1080/10705511.2022.2061494>, checks PLSc solutions for admissibility,
    and runs repeated k-fold cross-validation with identical folds for every
    method. Reports RMSE with Monte Carlo standard errors, the overfit ratio,
    the dispersion slope, benchmark comparisons, the cross-validated predictive
    ability test (CVPAT) of Liengaard et al. (2021) <doi:10.1111/deci.12445>,
    and prediction failures.
